### Global Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@teacherUsername = testuser
@teacherPassword = Password123!

@teacherToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
# Fake FCM token — real ones only come from an actual Android device via
# Firebase Messaging SDK, so this just exercises the register/unregister
# plumbing, not real push delivery.
@fakeDeviceToken = fake-fcm-token-1234567890abcdef

---

### 1. Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{teacherUsername}}", "password": "{{teacherPassword}}" }

### 2. Register Device Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/register-device
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{fakeDeviceToken}}" }

### 3. Register Same Token Again — should still 204 (upsert, no duplicate-key error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/register-device
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{fakeDeviceToken}}" }

### 4. Register Without a Token — should 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/register-device
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5. Unregister Device Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/unregister-device
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{fakeDeviceToken}}" }

### 6. Unregister Non-Existent Token — should still 204 (no-op, not an error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/unregister-device
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "some-token-that-was-never-registered" }